WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.550
- Every lawyer always puts
their client's interest first

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.266
and is always a paragon of virtue.

00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:07.380
(chuckles) All right, I
couldn't even say that

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.213
with this a straight face,

00:00:08.213 --> 00:00:10.560
but the vast majority of
attorneys serve their clients

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.820
with honor and distinction.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.940
Well, the majority. A
majority of lawyers...

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:15.990
No.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.650
Some lawyers serve their clients
with honor and distinction,

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.380
and yet, lawyers have long
been the target of jokes

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.120
and media portrayals that depict us

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.910
as a uniquely unethical occupation.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.650
- And as for your case, don't you worry.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.050
I've argued in front of
every judge in the state,

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.310
often as a lawyer.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.140
- But even though most lawyers

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.150
choose the straight and narrow path,

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.820
others have broken bad.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.560
So today let's not talk
about those good lawyers

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.700
you never hear about,

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.700
let's talk about when
lawyers have gone wild.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.421
- And the truth shall set you free!

00:00:49.421 --> 00:00:51.120
- So let's start with a
lawyer who defrauds, yes,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.970
a nine-year-old girl with grandpa's help.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.760
Now, one of the cardinal
duties of legal representation

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.220
is undivided loyalty to clients.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.130
Under this ethical mandate,
lawyers have a legal obligation

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.590
not to enrich themselves
to the client's detriment

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.200
and to zealously advocate
for a client's interests

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.850
above our own personal desires.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:13.020
But that's exactly what Vincent
J. Trimarco, Jr. did not do.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.370
He's a Long Island litigator

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.530
who conspired with client Gary Eriksen

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.380
to slowly steal $2 million of inheritance

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.480
from Eriksen's nine-year-old granddaughter

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.180
and Trimarco's client, Rebecca Schaefer.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.040
Now Miss Schaefer was
set to receive millions

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.600
from a federal wrongful death settlement

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.150
involving her father who
died at age 20 in jail

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.130
while serving a misdemeanor
for drug charges.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.800
From April 2012 through August 2017,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.140
Trimarco and the
co-conspirator grandfather

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.540
orchestrated a scheme to
steal millions of dollars

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.490
from a fatherless child.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.750
They purchased luxury vehicles,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.837
including a Ferrari
430 Spider for $200,000

00:01:45.837 --> 00:01:48.750
and a Jaguar XKR Convertible for $57,000,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.110
and they spent over $600,000
to purchase several properties

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.580
throughout Suffolk County, New York.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.720
And they even invested over
$800,000 of ill-gotten gains

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.940
in The Emporium, a now defunct nightclub

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.140
and music venue in New York

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.330
that Trimarco was at times part owner of.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.520
And while Mr. Trimarco must
have gotten his legal training

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.050
from the Lionel Hutz school of law,

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:09.180
Clearly the grandfather
learned his family skills

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.290
from Lucille Bluth.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.450
- Oh, don't give me that look.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.210
I happen to be a more
caring mother than most.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.590
- And in October 2017,

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:19.170
federal prosecutors
unveiled 19-count indictment

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.870
against Trimarco for conspiracy
to commit mail fraud,

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.130
wire fraud, money laundering,

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.280
and other charges related to
the multi-million dollar theft.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.800
Grandfather Eriksen, who
died before the investigation

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.500
was completed, was named as
an unindicted co-conspirator.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.560
But in October 2020, Trimarco
pleaded guilty to the charges.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.520
In announcing the sentence,

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.560
U.S. attorney Breon Peace outlined

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.570
why Trimarco's breach
of his fiduciary duty

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:40.920
to his client was so egregious.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.357
Quote, "Trimarco's theft of
a seven-figure inheritance

00:02:43.357 --> 00:02:45.907
"from a child so that he
could purchase luxury vehicles

00:02:45.907 --> 00:02:48.757
"and invest in real estate is
a disgraceful breach of trust

00:02:48.757 --> 00:02:51.457
"and betrayal of his time-honored
duties as an attorney.

00:02:51.457 --> 00:02:53.767
"His conduct is an affront to the courts,

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.387
"the bar, and the community at large.

00:02:55.387 --> 00:02:57.157
"Today's sentence should
serve as a warning

00:02:57.157 --> 00:02:59.257
"that this office will
prosecute corrupt attorneys

00:02:59.257 --> 00:03:00.337
"who abuse their positions

00:03:00.337 --> 00:03:02.190
"and break the law for personal gain."

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.680
And in December 2021,
Trimarco was sentenced

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:05.880
to 57 months in prison,

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.670
ordered to pay restitution
of $1.5 million,

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.400
and forfeit the amount of $1.5 million.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.630
And shortly after sentencing,

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.650
the New York Grievance Committee,

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.270
which regulates attorney
conduct in the state,

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.680
retroactively disbarred Trimarco

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.870
as of his October 2020 guilty plea.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.880
But it's not just lawyers
who have gone bad,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.840
it's also judges,

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.400
and that takes us to these shirtless judge

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.740
who sent explicit photos
of himself to the bailiff

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.950
and then impregnated a witness
in his judicial chambers.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.750
Now, judges have this reputation

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.970
for being stuffy,
humorless old men in robes,

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.730
but in the case of Judge
Wade Harper McCree,

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.250
who is neither old, stuffy, nor humorless,

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.010
he would still be a judge
if he had kept his robe on

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.810
because in 2012, Judge McCree was serving

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.820
on the Third Circuit Court
in Wayne County, Michigan,

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.070
where he specialized in
sexual misconduct cases.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.480
No, I'm not making that up.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.920
You would think that with that experience

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:50.753
he would've known better

00:03:50.753 --> 00:03:53.717
than send bare-chested photo
of himself to a female bailiff.

00:03:53.717 --> 00:03:54.600
(person screaming)

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.060
This is inappropriate workplace conduct,

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.730
and neither the bailiff, nor
her husband found it amusing.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.980
The judge, who was also married,

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.620
was confronted with a printout
of the photo by local news

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:08.217
by replying, "Hot dog. Yep, that's me."

00:04:13.874 --> 00:04:16.140
(sighs) McCree, whose father served

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.670
under President Jimmy Carter

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.800
as the second African
American solicitor general

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.270
in the United States' history,

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.580
was unbothered by the
misconduct allegation,

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.610
stating, quote, "I've
got no shame in my game."

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:29.070
Good God, man.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:32.640
But he later admitted to sending
the photo to other women.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.410
Now, Judge McCree might have been able

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.300
to weather this sexting scandal,

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.400
but his inability to keep it in his robe

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.310
led to a spectacular public downfall.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.860
While presiding over a
child support case in 2013,

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.140
Judge McCree repeatedly
used his judicial chambers

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.440
for extramarital trysts
with a witness in his case.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.330
- [Lawyer] Between May
and November of 2012,

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.420
did you engage in sexual
conduct with Judge McCree?

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.290
- Yes, I did.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.700
- Sneak the witness a cell phone

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.380
in violation of security protocol

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.660
so that he could regularly
text her during trial,

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.010
got the witness pregnant,

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.600
urged her to terminate the pregnancy,

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.660
and then repeatedly lied
about the episode under oath.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.400
- No, it's salesman's puffery.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.680
- Not surprisingly, the
judge was formally removed

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.210
from the bench in 2014,

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.280
barred from being a judge for six years,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.380
I don't know why only six years,

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:19.170
and following a three-year
suspension of his law license,

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:22.860
the shirtless judge's license
was reinstated in 2020.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.290
So now that McCree has
been given a second chance

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.570
at a legal practice, perhaps going forward

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:31.440
he could stand to have just a
little more shame in his game.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.090
But that takes us to the caveman lawyer

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:34.320
who stalked his ex-girlfriend,

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.270
repeatedly shoots her
office with a crossbow,

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.770
and got disbarred for it.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.830
Now what sets modern man apart
from Neanderthal ancestors

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.410
is the ability to work
out disputes using words

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.360
instead of brute force.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.470
Sometimes.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.020
But in the case of Steven A. Weinkauf,

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.820
this California caveman lawyer decided

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.470
that the way to address his hurt feelings

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:55.980
toward his lawyer ex-girlfriend
was not to use his words

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.090
but his crossbow,

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.100
and it cost him his law
license, his reputation,

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.350
and millions of dollars
because in the early 2010s,

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.600
Weinkauf began a romantic relationship

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.570
with fellow attorney
Adriana last name redacted

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.403
when they worked together

00:06:07.403 --> 00:06:09.570
in the San Francisco County
Public Guardian's office.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.580
The relationship ended in December 2013,

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.610
and while the girlfriend
moved on, Weinkauf did not.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.920
The girlfriend installed security
cameras at her law office

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.840
after finding crossbow arrows

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.640
shot into her building's windows

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.160
in April, June, and August of 2015.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.650
And in January 2017,
surveillance video showed

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:28.290
someone in a red Jeep firing
a gun at the building,

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:29.640
cracking a window.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.280
Five days later, the same
red Jeep drove by at night

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.290
and fired another crossbow at the office,

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.450
and the girlfriend was able
to identify her assailant

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.700
as none other than Weinkauf.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.520
Weinkauf was arrested and
convicted of felony stalking

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.160
with enhanced felonies
for using a deadly weapon.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.440
The state bar deemed this
offense moral turpitude

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.900
and Weinkauf was disbarred in 2020.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.180
That same year Weinkauf
was found civilly liable

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.370
for stalking, intentional
infliction of emotional distress,

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.830
and domestic violence
against his ex-girlfriend.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.630
At trial, Weinkauf admitted to shooting

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:00.960
the crossbow one time, but
denied the other incidents

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.870
because it was some other
crossbow-wielding maniac.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:04.830
But not surprisingly,

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:06.660
the jury did not believe Weinkauf's claim

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.840
of another crossbower
menacing the ex-girlfriend

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.030
and awarded her $1.3 million in damages,

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.880
plus over $900,000 in
attorney's fees and costs.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.100
In March 2022, the
California Court of Appeals

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.110
upheld the multimillion-dollar judgment.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.270
The takeaway here though
is while there may be

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.370
hypothetically situations

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:26.070
where a crossbow can solve your problems,

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:29.130
a broken heart is not one of those things.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.488
Obviously for that you need a trebuchet.

00:07:31.488 --> 00:07:34.655
(trebuchet whooshing)

00:07:37.983 --> 00:07:39.742
(projectile whooshing)

00:07:39.742 --> 00:07:42.000
(crowd cheering)

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.470
But that takes us to the Florida judge

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.940
who throws down with a public defender

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.100
and gets thrown off the bench.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.350
Because when a headline
begins with Florida man

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.940
or Florida woman, you
know you're about to read

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.996
something that's equal
parts bonkers, hilarious,

00:07:52.996 --> 00:07:56.723
and just a dash of "I'm so
glad that that's not me."

00:07:56.723 --> 00:08:00.360
(headlines thudding)

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.920
But when the headline is "Florida judge,"

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.920
well, it's all those
things ramped up to 11,

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.960
and such was the tale of John C. Murphy,

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.600
a Florida judge who decided
to settle a procedural dispute

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.330
with a public defender in the
most Floridian way possible,

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:13.950
by challenging him to a fist fight.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.420
Eh, now that I think about it,

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.790
I mean, duel, challenging
someone to a duel

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.350
is probably the most Floridian way,

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.720
but fist fight is a close second.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.341
- I demand satisfaction.

00:08:23.341 --> 00:08:24.174
(glove slapping)
- Oh!

00:08:24.174 --> 00:08:25.080
- I challenge you to a duel.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.280
- Hey, a duel?

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.200
- Anyway, on June 2nd, 2014,

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.030
Assistant Public Defender Andrew Weinstock

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.950
and Brevard County Judge John Murphy

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.710
we're engaged in a war of words
over Mr. Weinstock's refusal

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.020
to waive his client's
right to a speedy trial,

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.760
which is a very routine matter

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.800
that is typically resolved amicably

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.320
in open court with words.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.340
But not this judge.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.140
No, when Weinstock refused to waive

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:47.850
his client's speedy trial rights,

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.350
Judge Murphy exploded.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.330
- [Judge Murphy] If you wanna
fight, let's go out back

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.333
and I'll just beat your ass.
- Let's go right now.

00:08:55.239 --> 00:08:57.708
(attendees chattering)

00:08:57.708 --> 00:08:58.707
- [Judge Murphy] Ah! I'm gonna get you.

00:08:58.707 --> 00:08:59.957
You wanna (beep) with me.

00:09:00.826 --> 00:09:02.076
(attendees chattering)

00:09:02.076 --> 00:09:03.600
Do you? All right!

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.060
- But Weinstock stood his
ground against the irate jurist,

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.160
and that's when Judge
Murphy decided to turn

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.830
his pretrial hearing
into a trial by combat.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.510
Unfortunately, as
Weinstock would soon see,

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.850
Judge Murphy, a former colonel in the army

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:16.980
and Afghanistan veteran,
had plenty of experience

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.570
settling disputes on the battlefield.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.850
Weinstock follows Judge
Murphy out of the courtroom

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.050
and into the hallway

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:24.450
as sounds of a struggle
can be heard off camera.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.670
And according to reports,
a sheriff's deputy

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.530
witnessed the men gripping one another

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:31.470
around the collars of their
suit jackets while screaming.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.690
The Florida judge allegedly
punched Weinstock in the face

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:36.330
before a pair of deputies
broke up the fight.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.340
Weinstock was reassigned
to another courtroom

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.650
to avoid a second confrontation.

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:42.780
When Judge Murphy
returned to the courtroom,

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:46.440
because this is Florida, he
was greeted with laughter

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.238
and thunderous applause.

00:09:48.238 --> 00:09:51.571
(attendees applauding)

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:56.490
- [Judge Murphy] I will
catch my breath eventually.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:57.783
Man, I'm an old man.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.450
- But with Weinstock no longer present

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.950
to defend his clients,

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.830
Judge Murphy obtained speedy trial waivers

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.740
from Weinstock's unrepresented defendants,

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.110
probably because they
had just seen the judge

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.330
pummel the crap out of their lawyer.

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:14.940
- In bird culture, this
is considered a dick move.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.040
- But it's also what
we lawyer guys refer to

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.800
as a huge ethical violation.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.780
Judge Murphy issued a public apology,

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.670
enrolled in anger management classes,

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:25.920
and took a four-week paid leave of absence

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:29.010
and was reassigned from
criminal to civil cases.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:30.990
Weinstock resigned in protest

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:34.230
after Public Defender Blaise
Trettis declared his support

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.363
for Judge Murphy's return to the bench.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.120
Judge Murphy went viral for the video

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.310
and was dubbed the,
quote, "fighting judge,"

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:42.780
but not everyone was amused.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:45.330
In 2015, the Supreme Court of
Florida removed Judge Murphy

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.150
from the bench, overruling
the state disciplinary board,

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:50.640
which, again, I can't
emphasize this enough,

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.700
because it was Florida
only had recommended

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:56.880
a four-month suspension
and a $50,000 fine.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:57.847
The Court acknowledged, quote,

00:10:57.847 --> 00:11:00.277
"It is without question that
except for the June 2nd,

00:11:00.277 --> 00:11:04.140
"2014 incident, Judge Murphy
had been a good judge."

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:06.330
Nevertheless, the court
concluded that Judge Murphy had,

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:09.000
quote, "surrendered his
privilege" to serve as a judge

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.050
after threatening violence

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.330
against the attorney appearing before him,

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.070
fighting that attorney,

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:17.280
and then inducing the
attorney's unrepresented clients

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.020
to accept speedy trial waivers.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:21.307
Quote, "Judge Murphy's
total lack of self-control

00:11:21.307 --> 00:11:22.927
"became a national spectacle,

00:11:22.927 --> 00:11:24.667
"an embarrassment not
only to the judge himself,

00:11:24.667 --> 00:11:26.407
"but also to Florida's judicial system.

00:11:26.407 --> 00:11:28.807
"Given the clear erosion
of public confidence

00:11:28.807 --> 00:11:30.967
"in the judiciary cause by his misconduct,

00:11:30.967 --> 00:11:32.880
"removal is an appropriate sanction."

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.310
And I have to say if there's
one takeaway from this case

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:38.010
it's that not even the honor
of being an elected judge

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.500
is enough to overcome the
force that compels residents

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:44.940
of the Sunshine State to
transform into Florida man.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.470
But that takes us to a couple of lawyers

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.090
you might have heard something about.

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:49.620
- Good evening, America.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.450
We are Mark and Patty McCloskey.

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:53.490
- They are the Missouri
personal injury lawyers

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:56.190
who spent decades suing
everyone for everything,

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.740
then they waved their
guns at BLM protestors,

00:11:58.740 --> 00:11:59.790
became MAGA celebrities,

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:01.650
and then they sued even more people.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.320
Now, personal injury attorneys
are often referred to

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.000
as ambulance chasers

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.450
due to a reputation for
filing costly frivolous suits.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.370
But in the case of Missouri
personal injury lawyers

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.230
Patricia and Mark McCloskey,

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.340
it turns out all you need to do

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.350
is basically look at them the wrong way

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:17.640
and they'll sue you.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.006
♪ I'll sue ya ♪

00:12:19.006 --> 00:12:20.444
♪ I'll take all your money ♪

00:12:20.444 --> 00:12:23.130
♪ I'll sue ya if you
even look at me funny ♪

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.798
- Or they'll point
their guns at your face.

00:12:25.798 --> 00:12:27.009
♪ He'll sue ya ♪

00:12:27.009 --> 00:12:28.519
♪ He'll put a gun in your face ♪

00:12:28.519 --> 00:12:31.350
♪ She'll shoot ya probably
because of your race ♪

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.927
- Now, you've likely seen this
viral photo from June 2020

00:12:33.927 --> 00:12:36.630
when the McCloskeys pointed
firearms at BLM protesters

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.790
marching past their St Louis home.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.220
But that's not their
first public spectacle.

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:43.350
Here's how Jeremy Kohler
of the "St. Louis Dispatch"

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.570
described the couple following
a review of public records.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.647
Quote, "The McCloskeys are
almost always in conflict

00:12:47.647 --> 00:12:50.077
"with others, typically over
control of private property,

00:12:50.077 --> 00:12:51.817
"what people can do on that property,

00:12:51.817 --> 00:12:54.240
"and whose job it is to
make sure they do it."

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.490
Now, among there many, many legal fights,

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:58.320
it includes suing to obtain their home,

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:00.600
a castle originally
built by Adolphus Busch,

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.100
co-founder of Anheuser-Busch,

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:03.780
suing a man who sold them a Maserati

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:04.860
they claimed was supposed to come

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.570
with a box of hard-to-find parts,

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.840
and fighting their HOA to
acquire 1,100 square feet

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:12.330
of a triangle of lawn
designated as a common area

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:13.200
for the neighborhood.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.330
Now, one notable McCloskey dispute

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.710
bordered on cartoon villainy.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:20.070
In 2013, Mark McCloskey
allegedly destroyed beehives

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.810
placed outside his mansion's northern wall

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:24.600
by the neighboring Jewish
Central Reform Congregation,

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:25.980
then left a note saying

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:27.900
that if the mess wasn't cleaned up quickly

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:30.000
he'd seek a restraining
order and attorney's fees.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.920
The congregation was
planning to harvest the honey

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.720
and apples on the property
for the Jewish new year,

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:36.037
and according to Rabbi Susan Talve, quote,

00:13:36.037 --> 00:13:38.317
"The children were crying in school.

00:13:38.317 --> 00:13:39.960
"It was part of our curriculum."

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.120
Now, Mark McCloskey denied
destroying the hives,

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.520
and a Snopes investigation
was unable to confirm

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:45.762
who killed the bees.

00:13:45.762 --> 00:13:47.390
- No! Not the bees!

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:48.510
Not the bees!

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.280
- Now flash-forward to June 2020

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.350
when a group of several
hundred BLM demonstrators

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.750
marched on the home of St.
Louis Mayor Lyda Krewson.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.610
Mayor Krewson had
triggered fierce backlash

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:58.560
when during a Facebook Live post

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.150
she read the full names and addresses

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.490
of George Floyd protestors
who had written letters

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.920
encouraging her to defund
police departments.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.480
Critics accused her of doxing critics

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:08.850
to open them up to public
harassment and retaliation.

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:11.940
And on June 28th, protestors
marched toward Krewson's home

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.800
along a street called Portland Place

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.930
which is blocked with heavy iron gates

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.430
and signs marked "Private property."

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:19.140
But one of the houses on Portland Place

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:21.450
is a Renaissance-style palazzo owned by,

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:24.150
you guessed it, Patricia
and Mark McCloskey.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.790
When the demonstrators crossed
paths with the McCloskeys,

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:29.160
the pair countered the
protestors' First Amendment rights

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.440
by threatening them with
their Second Amendment rights.

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:33.900
Mr. McCloskey stepped onto
his patio holding a rifle

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:36.150
and yelled, "Get the hell
out of my neighborhood,"

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.890
and, "Private property, get out."

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.600
After McCloskey brandished his rifle,

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.700
Mrs. McCloskey then came
out of the door barefoot

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.230
wielding a small silver pistol

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.970
and aimed it directly
to the demonstrators.

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:47.040
The entire confrontation
lasted about 12 minutes,

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.480
after which the protestors converged

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:51.120
on Mayor Krewson's home for
several hours of protest.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.760
But the McCloskeys
immediately became the couple

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:56.400
who launched a thousand memes and lawsuits

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.680
because the McCloskeys
sued the photographer

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.090
who took their viral photograph,

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:02.430
the online retailer who used
that photo to sell products

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:04.020
with their unflattering captions.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:05.670
And while the couple
became MAGA celebrities-

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.050
- They were gonna be beat up badly

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.910
and the house was gonna
be totally ransacked

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.140
and probably burned down,

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.120
like they try to burn down churches.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.490
- In June 2021, the
McCloskeys pleaded guilty

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:15.810
to misdemeanor offenses,

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:19.230
Mark for fourth-degree
assault with a $750 fine

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.720
and Patricia for harassment
with a $2,000 fine.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.640
The couple was required
to surrender their guns

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:26.550
for destruction, and Mark
McCloskey wasted no time

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:30.270
in blaming the person actually
responsible for all of this,

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:31.260
George Soros.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:34.530
But in August of 2021,
Missouri Governor Mike Parson

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.560
pardoned the McCloskeys,
which he had promised to do

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.030
if they were convicted.

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:40.410
The McCloskeys, true to form,

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.870
then immediately sued the city,
the sheriff, and the state

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:44.460
alleging the pardon entitled them

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.520
to have their guns returned
and fines refunded.

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.640
But in February of 2022,
the Missouri Supreme Court

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:52.290
subjected the McCloskeys law licenses

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:54.120
to a one-year probationary period.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.620
After the ruling, Mark McCloskey said

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.870
that he was disappointed the
court disciplined him at all

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:59.430
and announced he was considering asking

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.710
the U.S. Supreme Court to review the case.

